From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thomas Glanzmann <thomas@glanzmann.de>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 07:40:47 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: display: apple,dcp: accept K-board panel
 compatibles

The PROLED MacBook Pros are K boards (K114s/c, K116s/c). Like the J
boards, their panel node can name the board before the generic
compatible: the K116s uses "apple,panel-k116", "apple,panel". Accept
apple,panel-k<n> where apple,panel-j<n> is accepted.

Signed-off-by: Thomas Glanzmann <thomas@glanzmann.de>
(cherry picked from commit 3adc985b5a61d091eb869343c9b29e0eb1407cc0)
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/apple,dcp.yaml | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/apple,dcp.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/apple,dcp.yaml
index c18292bf4..d0bc33404 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/apple,dcp.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/apple,dcp.yaml
@@ -392,10 +392,10 @@ properties:
               - apple,panel
               - apple,panel-mini-led
           - items:
-              - pattern: '^apple,panel-j[0-9]+$'
+              - pattern: '^apple,panel-[jk][0-9]+$'
               - const: apple,panel
           - items:
-              - pattern: '^apple,panel-j[0-9]+$'
+              - pattern: '^apple,panel-[jk][0-9]+$'
               - const: apple,panel-mini-led
               - const: apple,panel
       width-mm:
